  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 100 PM CST Tue Nov 3 2026\n\nA few showers may linger in the north as lingering moisture feeds \ninto the area. Once the low clears Iowa, flow aloft will begin to \ncome from the north and west. The abundant moisture transport into \nthe area that has helped drive the showers will be choked off, and \ncooler, drier air will set in. The Extreme Forecast Index (EFI), \nwhich has been consistently highlighting the area as having above \nnormal highs and lows is starting to back off on this signal. By the \nweekend, overnight lows look to dip into the 30s with the potential \nfor northern Iowa to see lows in the upper 20s.",
